Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayDomain", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"474c2681-d0ce-724a-8479-3ebf0b0f7ba0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayDomain", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"9c3805a1-29d9-8441-98a8-a5a77b7effee"],
 " ",
 "gives the narrowest recognized value domain containing every entry of arr, \
or \"Expression\" if the entries lie in none of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"058a9870-5ae4-0c4e-b779-8accd297fb89"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"634d6ff1-0e42-ac48-a289-4e838a9c48ea"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \"Real\" \
and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9cef106c-5765-474b-8817-475a63f9275c"],

Cell["\<\
\"Boolean\" means the entries are True and False. Entries 0 and 1 are \
integers, and the elements of the two-element field are FiniteField[2, 1].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"122b4df0-4703-ae4d-8c1d-d3da0b85d1be"],

Cell["\<\
It is computed from the entries, not declared: an array is not told what it \
is made of. An array whose entries answer to none of the recognized domains \
is an array of expressions, which is a perfectly good array; generated \
symbolic entries and labels are both of that kind.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"45b1b1b8-4ca2-0249-98a2-e8e192e60753"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is computed rather than stored, it costs a pass over the entries \
to ask.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"822c65ed-bec7-2b41-972f-b11369c4155a"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"df081e51-5e18-a142-adb9-fc0dfda77419"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[#] & /@ {{True, False}, {1, 2}, {1/2, 3}, {1.5, 2}, \
{1 + I, 2}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e607006d-dd68-e548-8674-2dd48af9c835"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Boolean\"\>", ",", "\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rational\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Complex\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionU\
UID->"cb641809-86bb-ca4a-bf1a-224d535f1a3a"],

Cell["Entries of a finite field:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"02d834ab-f730-f744-9ecd-ff689de867f6"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[{FiniteField[2, 1][0], FiniteField[2, 1][1]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"001f0c06-c0ee-5147-9581-fa11bd4554ca"],

